{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes","id":1459239,"title":"W20 Jam Weapon and Fetishes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T19:59:00-07:00","id":1459239,"title":"W20 Jam Weapon and Fetishes","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Does the gift <i>Jam Weapon</i>, disable weapon fetishes? I am particularly interested on Klaives and the <i>Hunter\u2019s Talons</i> fetish.<br /> <br /> I am almost positive that Klaives are affected but unsure about the <i>Hunter\u2019s Talons</i> as those are claw complements and not manufactured but provided by an Incarna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jam Weapon (Level One) \u2014 The Child may <b>stop </b><br /> <b>any Weaver-born weapons</b> from working within the range<br /> of his voice. A dove-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> System: The Garou shouts an ancient word of power<br /> and grace and spends a Gnosis point. The player rolls<br /> Willpower against a difficulty of highest Willpower of<br /> any armed individual within earshot. For each success, <b>all<br /> manufactured weapons will not function </b>for one turn. <b>This<br /> includes guns, crossbows, flame-throwers, and even knives<br /> and swords, which refuse to cut.</b> <b>Natural weapons (such as<br /> claws) and natural objects appropriated as weapons (such<br /> as rocks or naturally-fallen tree limbs) are unaffected.</b> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-07-2021, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T20:32:16-07:00","id":1459241,"title":"","content":"Easy part first: Hunter's Talons clearly wouldn't fall under the Gift. Not only do they come from an Incarna, but Jam Weapon explicitly doesn't apply to natural items like branches or rocks in that are found in the environment. Hunter's Talons are made from bits of metal that &quot;naturally&quot; occur in Rorg's Realm.<br /> <br /> For a Klaive.... there's enough ambiguity in the phrasing here to go either way. W20 dropped the &quot;moving parts&quot; aspect of things to make it work against blades, but the Gift stresses Weaver tools and manufacturing. You could interpret that any tool is manufactured, and thus a Klaive would be affected. You could also interpret this not to apply to &quot;artisanal&quot; weapons that are custom crafted using traditional methods that don't rise to the Weaver-ish-ness of manufacturing; thus most Fetish weapons like Klaives wouldn't be impacted.<br /> <br /> I personally tend towards the second simply because it's a level 1 Gift and being able to shut down powerful magical items like that with no extra effort strikes me as a bigger impact than the Gift should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T20:56:01-07:00","id":1459244,"title":"","content":"Funny enough we disagree on the difficulty of the questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes?p=1459241#post1459241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy part first: Hunter's Talons clearly wouldn't fall under the Gift. Not only do they come from an Incarna, but Jam Weapon explicitly doesn't apply to natural items like branches or rocks in that are found in the environment. Hunter's Talons are made from bits of metal that &quot;naturally&quot; occur in Rorg's Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am doubting on this item, the introductory text to the section makes clear that Garou can <i>not </i>make the Talons and that Incarna and their servants provide them, perhaps bypassing the manufacture part.<br /> <br /> However, the text of the fetish states that the Talons are &quot;<i>like </i><i>some sort of clawed gauntlet</i>&quot; and therefore a weapon, plus the art on the book makes them look very elaborated (the manufactured part?), so the providence of the material is not the only factor here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes?p=1459241#post1459241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Klaive.... there's enough ambiguity in the phrasing here to go either way. W20 dropped the &quot;moving parts&quot; aspect of things to make it work against blades, but the Gift stresses Weaver tools and manufacturing. You could interpret that any tool is manufactured, and thus a Klaive would be affected. You could also interpret this not to apply to &quot;artisanal&quot; weapons that are custom crafted using traditional methods that don't rise to the Weaver-ish-ness of manufacturing; thus most Fetish weapons like Klaives wouldn't be impacted.<br /> <br /> I personally tend towards the second simply because it's a level 1 Gift and being able to shut down powerful magical items like that with no extra effort strikes me as a bigger impact than the Gift should have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I am certain it works: as it mentions <i>all </i>manufactured weapons, I am of the opinion that Klaives do not work under the gift effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-08-2021, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T21:43:43-07:00","id":1459251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes?p=1459241#post1459241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally tend towards the second simply because it's a level 1 Gift and being able to shut down powerful magical items like that with no extra effort strikes me as a bigger impact than the Gift should have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I almost agree, if that was the case the gift would have phrasing excluding other handmade weapons regardless of being a fetish, but it doesn't.<br /> <br /> But I'm not worried for a simpler reason: the gift stops the Klaive from cutting, but the Klaive doesn't cause Aggravated damage because it cuts, it causes Aggravated damage because of its magic. The gift affects the weapon, not the magic (technically the war spirit inside it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  typo 09-08-2021, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T00:23:08-07:00","id":1459261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes?p=1459244#post1459244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here I am certain it works: as it mentions <i>all </i>manufactured weapons, I am of the opinion that Klaives do not work under the gift effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is... which definition of manufactured? There's a lot, with a range of implication, and the book doesn't really give much guidance on where to go with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1459239-w20-jam-weapon-and-fetishes?p=1459251#post1459251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I almost agree, if that was the case the gift would have phrasing excluding other handmade weapons regardless of being a fetish, but it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>My concern is how potent Jam Weapon is for a Rank 1 Gift. IME it's already really powerful. You can turn First Teams into mooks with a good roll as all their weapons stop working (and they're using manufactured weapons regardless of ambiguity of that term) because even a few successes is enough for a halfway competent pack to rip most of them to shreds.<br /> <br /> Not having it work on most Fetish weapons doesn't stop it from being incredibly useful, while being able to shut down most Fetish weapons is fairly ridiculous for Gift of it's level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm not worried for a simpler reason: the gift stops the Klaive from cutting, but the Klaive doesn't cause Aggravated damage because it cuts, it causes Aggravated damage because of its magic. The gift affects the weapon, not the magic (technically the war spirit inside it). </div> </div> </div>If a Klaive can't roll damage, it can't deal damage. It does Agg damage while Jam Weapon is active, but what does that matter if it does zero damage on a hit?<br /> <br /> And while Ibeaumanjor is specifically asking about Klaives, there's plenty of other Fetish weapons out there. Most of them rely on dealing damage in someway to be relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T07:58:05-07:00","id":1459306,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> What do you think of the points I made about the Talons when I answered Heavy Arms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T13:46:14-07:00","id":1459338,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;like&quot; before &quot;some sort&quot; is meant to indicate that it isn't a gauntlet, but for claws, it just acts in a similar fashion. If a Fetish was made of a natural tree branch but acted like a baseball bat, it wouldn't be a baseball bat and shouldn't be treated as a manufactured baseball bat; it's a natural stick.<br /> <br /> The art is... art. It's meant to be evocative and inspirational, not a way to judge the rules. Art is generally commissioned long before the text is finalized, and the artists rarely have the full context of the image (esp. smaller pieces like that one). I'd infer that an artist got a note to draw a werewolf with a metal gauntlet, and thus we see something befitting Crinos plate armor instead of something you'd expect to see made of the metallic chunks of asteroid collision debris. As such, I don't usually give weight to it unless there's a very compelling reason to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T18:18:18-07:00","id":1459383,"title":"","content":"On the matter of the Fetishes, I consider that the spirits/magic is able to overcome the gift anyways. That's the essence of what I meant with the damage, the war spirit inside won't be deterred and the Klaive will cause its damage normally. This is a way of going through its effectiveness without houseruling the Gift, and my first suggestion is usually how to deal with things with no or minimum houseruling.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I agree it is exceedingly good for a level 1 gift. Indeed it is exceedingly good even for a level 2 gift, as written.<br /> <br /> The Talons are spiritual creations. They can look however you want and still not be affected by Weapon Jam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}